## Comments can be added to any line in a .lang file by starting the line with the '#' character.
##
## Comments can also be added after a key and value definition on the same line.
## However, they must be separated by a 'tab' character.
##
## The format for a key and value definition is "key=value".
##
## It is recommended that you use a tab character to separate your key and value definition.
## This will allow you to align all the values in your .lang file.
##
## For example:
##
## key.name.1=Value 1
## key.name.2=Value 2
##
## You can also use color codes in your lang file.
## For example:
##
## key.name.3=§eValue 3
##
## This will make "Value 3" appear in yellow text in the game.
##
## A list of all the color codes can be found here:
## https://minecraft.fandom.com/wiki/Formatting_codes
